module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionRingVeroneseChart.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionRingProjGoodOpen.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionExtension.Ample
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.MorphismToProjUniversal

/-!
# The two hypotheses of Stacks Tag 01N8 at the section ring of an ample module

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` an ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module, `S = Γ_*(X, L)` the graded section
ring of Stacks Tag 01CV and `f : X ⟶ Proj S` the canonical morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ. Stacks
Tag 01N8, in the form `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.existsUnique_pair`, is
stated for a scheme `Y`, a degree `d > 0`, an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module and a Veronese datum
`ψ : S^{(d)} → Γ_*(Y, ·)`, under one hypothesis: that the nonvanishing opens `Y_{ψ(g)}`,
`g ∈ S_d`, cover `Y`. At the section ring's own Veronese datum
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.sectionRingVeronese` that hypothesis is a statement
about `X` and `L` alone, and this file discharges it.

It also builds the **lift of the canonical morphism through the degree-`d` open** `U_d ⊆ Proj S`
of Stacks Tag 01N5, which is the shape Tag 01N8's conclusion is stated at: the `Pair` of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSectionsUnique.Pair` has a morphism into `U_d` as its first
component, so comparing it with `f` needs `f` factored through `U_d`.

Both come from the same source: **the degree-`d` powers of `L` are generated by global sections
once `d` is large**, which is the first half of clause (7) of Stacks Tag 01Q3
(`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_isAmple`). Generation in degree `d`
says exactly that the opens `X_a`, `a ∈ Γ(X, L ^⊗ d)`, cover `X`, and from that single covering
statement both hypotheses follow:

* `X_a = X_{ψ(a)}` for the Veronese datum, by
  `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.nonvanishingOpen_pow` in degree one together with
  `Stacks.SectionExtension.nvLocus_powSec_one`, so the covering is the generation hypothesis;
* `X_a` is the preimage of the standard open `D₊(a)` under `f` (clause (1) of Tag 01PZ), and
  `D₊(a) ⊆ U_d` for a degree-`d` element, so the covering makes the preimage of `U_d` all of `X`
  and `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.lift` produces the factorization.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.degreeLift` — **the canonical morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ,
  lifted through `U_d`.** Its composite with the open immersion is `projHomOfIsAmple` on the nose
  (`degreeLift_comp_ι`, `toProj_degreeLift`).

## Main results

* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.iSup_nvOpen_eq_top_of_isFinGen` — generation of `L ^⊗ n` by
  global sections, read as a covering of `X` by the nonvanishing opens of the degree-`n` part of
  the section ring.
* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.exists_forall_iSup_nvOpen_eq_top` — that covering holds in
  every sufficiently large degree, for `L` ample. This is the one place ampleness is spent.
* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.iSup_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection_eq_top` — **the generation
  hypothesis `hgen` of Stacks Tag 01N8** for the section ring's Veronese datum.
* `Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart.projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_degreeOpen` — the preimage of `U_d`
  under the canonical morphism is all of `X`.

## Implementation notes

**The covering is indexed by `Γ(X, L ^⊗ d)`, the generation hypothesis by `S_d`.** The two index
types are additively the same — `S_d` is the image of the former under `DirectSum.of`,
`Stacks.ExternalGrading.summandEquiv` — but they are not the same type, and the supremum over the
larger index type is only ever bounded below here, by `le_iSup_of_le` at the element
`DirectSum.of _ d a`. No surjectivity of the comparison is needed in either statement.

**`X_{a¹}` is `X_a` and that is not a definitional matter.** The Veronese datum's trivializing
section at `a` is the power `Stacks.SectionExtension.powSec L a 1`, a section of `L ^⊗ (d · 1)`,
and `d · 1` is not the term `d`; `Stacks.SectionExtension.nvLocus_powSec_one` is the equality of
the two nonvanishing loci, which is what carries the covering across.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CV)

## What is not done here

**No pair is produced.** This file supplies the two inputs; instantiating Tag 01N8 at them, and
identifying the resulting morphism with `projHomOfIsAmple`, is the sibling
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionRingVeroneseChart/Pair.lean`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite MonoidalCategory
open Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance (grading nvOpen nvLocus)
open Stacks.GradedSections (powSections sectionRing)
open Stacks.NonvanishingOpen (nonvanishingOpen)
open Stacks.SectionExtension (powSec)
open Stacks.TensorPowers (natTensorPow)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios
open AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (degreeOpen)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj (toProj basicOpen_le_degreeOpen)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal (psiSection nonvanishingOpen_psiSection)

universe u

namespace Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart

section Monoidal

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemePreadditive
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeTensorRightAdditive

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (L : X.Modules) [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-! ### Generation in a degree as a covering of `X` -/

/-- **Where `L ^⊗ n` is generated by global sections the opens `X_a`, `a ∈ S_n`, cover `X`.**
Pointwise, `Stacks.SectionRingProjGoodOpen.exists_powSections_mem_nvLocus_of_isFinGen`. -/
theorem iSup_nvOpen_eq_top_of_isFinGen {n : ℕ}
    (h : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModule X L (n : ℤ))) :
    (⨆ a : powSections L n, nvOpen L a) = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top fun x _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ :=
    Stacks.SectionRingProjGoodOpen.exists_powSections_mem_nvLocus_of_isFinGen L h x
  refine Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨a, ?_⟩
  have hx : x ∈ (nvOpen L a : Set X) := by
    rw [Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.coe_nvOpen]; exact ha
  exact hx

/-- **For `L` ample the opens `X_a`, `a ∈ S_n`, cover `X` in every sufficiently large degree.**
This is where ampleness is spent, through the first half of clause (7) of Stacks Tag 01Q3
(`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_isAmple`): the tensor powers of `L` are
generated by finitely many global sections in all degrees above some `n₀`, and
`iSup_nvOpen_eq_top_of_isFinGen` turns generation in a degree into the covering. -/
theorem exists_forall_iSup_nvOpen_eq_top (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) :
    ∃ n₀ : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, n₀ ≤ n → (⨆ a : powSections L n, nvOpen L a) = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨m₀, hm₀⟩ := Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isEventuallyFinGenPowers_of_isAmple L hL
  refine ⟨m₀.toNat, fun n hn => iSup_nvOpen_eq_top_of_isFinGen L (hm₀ (n : ℤ) ?_)⟩
  exact le_trans (Int.self_le_toNat m₀) (by exact_mod_cast hn)

/-- An open of `X` containing every `X_a`, `a ∈ Γ(X, L ^⊗ d)`, is `⊤` once these cover `X`. -/
private theorem eq_top_of_forall_nvOpen_le {d : ℕ} {U : X.Opens}
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) (h : ∀ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a ≤ U) :
    U = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.mpr (hcov.symm.le.trans (iSup_le h))

/-! ### The generation hypothesis of Stacks Tag 01N8 -/

/-- **The generation hypothesis of Stacks Tag 01N8 for the section ring's Veronese datum.** The
nonvanishing opens `X_{ψ(g)}`, `g ∈ S_d`, cover `X` as soon as the opens `X_a`,
`a ∈ Γ(X, L ^⊗ d)`, do.

The nonvanishing open of `ψ(g)` is that of the datum's trivializing section at `g` in degree one
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismToProjUniversal.nonvanishingOpen_psiSection`), which is
`X_{a¹} = X_a` by `nonvanishingOpen_pow` and `Stacks.SectionExtension.nvLocus_powSec_one`. Only
the elements `g = DirectSum.of _ d a` of `S_d` are used, so the supremum over all of `S_d` is
bounded below rather than computed. -/
theorem iSup_nonvanishingOpen_psiSection_eq_top (d : ℕ)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    (⨆ g : grading L d, nonvanishingOpen X (natTensorPow L d)
        (psiSection (grading L) (sectionRingVeronese L d) g)) = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_of_forall_nvOpen_le L hcov fun a => ?_
  refine le_iSup_of_le ⟨DirectSum.of (powSections L) d a,
    Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_summand d a⟩ ?_
  have h1 : nvOpen L (powSec L a 1) = nvOpen L a :=
    Opens.ext (by
      rw [Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.coe_nvOpen, Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.coe_nvOpen,
        Stacks.SectionExtension.nvLocus_powSec_one])
  rw [nonvanishingOpen_psiSection (grading L) (sectionRingVeronese L d), nonvanishingOpen_pow,
    h1]

/-! ### The canonical morphism factors through the degree-`d` open -/

/-- **The preimage of the degree-`d` open `U_d` of Stacks Tag 01N5 under the canonical morphism of
Stacks Tag 01PZ is all of `X`**, as soon as the opens `X_a`, `a ∈ Γ(X, L ^⊗ d)`, cover `X`.
Clause (1) of Tag 01PZ (`…projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_projBasicOpen`) identifies `X_a` with the
preimage of `D₊(a)`, and `D₊(a) ⊆ U_d` because `a` has degree `d`. -/
theorem projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_degreeOpen (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL ⁻¹ᵁ degreeOpen (grading L) d = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_of_forall_nvOpen_le L hcov fun a => ?_
  rw [← Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_projBasicOpen L hL a hd]
  exact Scheme.Hom.preimage_mono _
    (basicOpen_le_degreeOpen (grading L)
      ⟨DirectSum.of (powSections L) d a, Stacks.ExternalGrading.of_mem_summand d a⟩)

/-- **The canonical morphism of Stacks Tag 01PZ, lifted through the degree-`d` open `U_d`.** The
open immersion `U_d ⟶ Proj S` has the image of `projHomOfIsAmple` in its range by
`projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_degreeOpen`, so `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion.lift` factors the
morphism through it. This is the shape Stacks Tag 01N8's pair is stated at. -/
def degreeLift (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    X ⟶ (degreeOpen (grading L) d).toScheme :=
  IsOpenImmersion.lift (degreeOpen (grading L) d).ι
    (Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL) (by
      rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
      rintro y ⟨x, rfl⟩
      exact (projHomOfIsAmple_preimage_degreeOpen L hL hd hcov).ge (Opens.mem_top x))

/-- The lift of the canonical morphism, composed with the open immersion of `U_d`, is the
canonical morphism. -/
@[reassoc] theorem degreeLift_comp_ι (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    degreeLift L hL hd hcov ≫ (degreeOpen (grading L) d).ι
      = Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL :=
  IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac _ _ _

/-- The lift of the canonical morphism, read back as a morphism into `Proj S`, is the canonical
morphism. This is `degreeLift_comp_ι` at the spelling
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.toProj` that Stacks Tag 01N8's statements use. -/
theorem toProj_degreeLift (hL : Stacks.Ample.IsAmple X L) {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (hcov : (⨆ a : powSections L d, nvOpen L a) = ⊤) :
    toProj (grading L) (degreeLift L hL hd hcov)
      = Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple L hL :=
  degreeLift_comp_ι L hL hd hcov

end Monoidal

end Stacks.SectionRingVeroneseChart

end
